"shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"3cT6KPlkOQGZv2Lk7p9_1A","review_id":"zlVk09S0VSIWgX3lB5Owfw","date":"2016-09-05T23:09:13","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9423805475234985,"text_excerpt":"I have been to NOLA many times and I just discovered this place. I am so glad that I did. The candy that I had was really good. They have a wide variety of chocolates, pralines, fudge, taffy, etc. I tried the peanut butter/cayenne truffle, praline truffle, triple chocolate truffle, s'mores, rum praline and maple praline. The s'mores was my fave by far. Chocolate covered graham crackers with marshmallow fluff filling...AMAZING!! The \"kick\" of the cayenne in the truffle was a nice touch, but may not be for everyone, so just be aware of that. The triple chocolate truffle was the best of the ones that I tried, although they have many other flavors available. Of the pralines, the rum was aweso..."},{"business_id":"3cT6KPlkOQGZv2Lk7p9_1A","review_id":"iG21i9JQawpnxRPgXStlUg","date":"2013-09-02T23:29:14","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9358855485916138,"text_excerpt":"What an amazing candy store. You feel welcome and happy being in here. They have tons of samples and are happy to have you taste everything. The staff is so friendly and helpful. Everything was so damn good. The Mississippi mud, the maple praline, and the chocolate praline were my favorite. The stuff is not very cheap, but it is great quality, so it is worth it."},{"business_id":"3cT6KPlkOQGZv2Lk7p9_1A","review_id":"iSSuo7WlnFuQJAKPOkCVjQ","date":"2017-04-06T03:14:43","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9358502626419067,"text_excerpt":"You will see a lot of bakeries/ candy shops in the French Quarter advertising pralines. They are basically cookies made out of nuts and caramelized sugar. Laura's uses pecans. If I had to describe the pralines, they are in between a cookie and brittle. They are crunchy but soft enough to be considered a cookie. I tried samples at a couple of spots and Laura's Candies definitely had the ones I favored. I loved the traditional and chocolate flavors. They are about $2 each and $24 for a dozen. I bought a box as a gift to bring home to my family. Of course, they are much better if you eat them within the first day or two. If you are visiting New Orleans and looking for recommendations, feel f..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"3cT6KPlkOQGZv2Lk7p9_1A","photo_id":"vm-EKAsh--hm8K_6LcrpSg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/vm-EKAsh--hm8K_6LcrpSg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8909378051757812},{"business_id":"3cT6KPlkOQGZv2Lk7p9_1A","photo_id":"KjQbxRMsHIFqAUTBvHxyOA","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/KjQbxRMsHIFqAUTBvHxyOA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8475762009620667},{"business_id":"3cT6KPlkOQGZv2Lk7p9_1A","photo_id":"H_FmRCpWiBBPRGaZDrGw8w","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/H_FmRCpWiBBPRGaZDrGw8w.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7709707021713257},{"business_id":"3cT6KPlkOQGZv2Lk7p9_1A","photo_id":"Yc5QUuoRTL97wuC4X-6-fg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/Yc5QUuoRTL97wuC4X-6-fg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7547405958175659},{"business_id":"3cT6KPlkOQGZv2Lk7p9_1A","photo_id":"4Y7xciTQ7SuxsBWHspFqsg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/4Y7xciTQ7SuxsBWHspFqsg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7366153001785278}]},"notebook_case":null}
